      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5a3ad7fd682bb9742d24a0f2",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "I am weary of community mods and possible social implications, but 1000x more weary of nasty out of control troll behavior.\n\nI have a bit more power than most in The Pug as it stands, and it makes me uncomfortable wielding it sometimes. I would hope those that are deputized take great care and are held to strict standards of recording incidents just like current VRC mods are.\n\nFor a minor example of social dynamics that might be introduced with such a role, consider that a deputized mod would probably have access to all public instances no matter how full they are. This could be used as a social advantage to get friends access to full rooms. Minor things like this along with others can end up adding up to a social dynamic worth considering when it comes to deputized community members.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
