      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "There's a lot of good research on this subject in the gaming community. Its not the same, but there is overlap. Some things might be easy - like suggestions on the load screen akin to being a better team player could fit here.  It's minor, but easy to implement and hits the issue of fairness when someone is addressed.  A deeper look bigger ideas can be found here:\n\nhttps://www.gamasutra.com/view/news/260663/Video_Reducing_antisocial_behavior_in_games_through_smart_design.php   (this is a GDC talk by Ben, with a PhD in psychology and years of game research exp  :)\n\nalso for the old timers... (the fluffy bunny story)\n\nhttp://habitatchronicles.com/2007/03/the-untold-history-of-toontowns-speedchat-or-blockchattm-from-disney-finally-arrives/\n\nbest wishes for the new year\n\n- SteveG  (who had a DK1, left for a while, just came back ... and yes was disappointed by the conversations around me)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
